  "claim": "The defending champion in the 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles of France, called \"the best volleyer on tour\", defeated Juan Martín del Potro an Argentinian professional.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Michaël Llodra. Sentence: He is a successful doubles player with three Grand Slam championships and an Olympic silver medal, and has also had success in singles, winning five career titles and gaining victories over Novak Djokovic, Juan Martín del Potro, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević and John Isner.\nPage: Juan Martín del Potro. Sentence: Juan Martín del Potro (] , born 23 September 1988), also known as Delpo is an Argentinian professional tennis player who is currently ranked world No. 24 in men's singles by the Association of Tennis Professionals (ATP).\nPage: 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles. Sentence: Michaël Llodra was the defending champion, but lost in the second round to Gaël Monfils.",
